{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/docset at 2f2325f8499cbe704e2589632e5b30fd167568cf. The no-workroom skip is pinned and made immune to an inherited Git environment, on a chain that can be signed over.\n\nWHAT IS HERE. One new file, internal/docset/no_workroom_test.go, and nothing else. It asserts the docset gate skips explicitly with the exact no-workroom reason when run in a checkout holding no workroom, rather than failing or passing while measuring nothing. The gate has two skips and only the reason distinguishes them, so the test matches it through a named constant rather than accepting any skip. withoutGitEnvironment strips GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE and GIT_COMMON_DIR before the subprocess runs.\n\nThe content is byte-identical to the substantively approved d77044c4 version, verified by diff against d77044c4:internal/docset/no_workroom_test.go rather than by inspection.\n\nWHY THIS COMMIT EXISTS, which is the only thing that changed. The previous chain rested on records ruled out as stale or superseded — e6f0ad20, 38a325e9, the candidates 6b3237a9, d6eb003b and 13a1204c, and the reviews c08d02ec and b5a35534. The work was sound and its provenance was not, and a verdict signed over that lineage would inherit it. This artifact rests on nothing but request 02f2839f, my promise be03b558, and the live shipped predecessor 596cd629 whose commit 0f215b43 is an ancestor of main. I read the bases back off the fold after recording rather than trusting the list I typed, because I filed a record earlier today claiming a succession the fold had refused.\n\nHOSTILE-ENVIRONMENT PROOF, both halves, because only the pair means anything. With GIT_DIR and GIT_WORK_TREE pointed at this repository the focused test passes in 0.220s. With the stripping replaced by plain os.Environ() and the same environment set, it fails — and the failure names the mechanism: the subprocess resolved the real workroom and took the genesis-mismatch skip instead. So the stripping is what keeps the test in the no-workroom case, and the reason constant is what refuses the wrong skip; without the constant that mutation would pass silently on the other skip. Mutation reverted, worktree verified clean, head unchanged at 2f2325f8.\n\nGATES at this exact head: internal/docset uncached 118.575s, full go test ./... with zero failures, go vet clean, go build clean, git diff --check clean, git merge-tree against main 27603774 clean.\n\nSUCCESSION. 596cd629 stays live: it describes what main carries, and the guarded merge is what should retire it. The stale candidate 13a1204c is retired against this record now that this replacement exists, in that order, so the path is never left without a candidate.","body":{"commit":"2f2325f8499cbe704e2589632e5b30fd167568cf","path":"internal/docset"}}